 "id": "y11-8-1-ops",
 "label": "8.1 L4: Relational and Logical Operators",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "do-now",
   "label": "Do Now: Arithmetic Operators (1 of 2)",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y11op-do-now",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Arithmetic Operators (1 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does a program write ^ and not a small raised number, like in maths?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Code is typed on one line. ^ shows the power on that line.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">From 8.1 L3. Cambridge IGCSE 0478/22, November 2025, Question 1.</p><div id=\"y11op-do-now\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "Tick one box to complete this sentence. The result of the arithmetic operation 4 ^ 2 is",
     "options": [
      "2",
      "8",
      "16",
      "42"
     ],
     "correct": 2,
     "explain": "4 ^ 2 means 4 raised to the power of 2: 4 * 4."
    }
   ],
   "walkthrough": {
    "title": "Walk me through it: raised to the power of",
    "steps": [
     {
      "text": "We will work out <strong>3 ^ 4</strong>. Your question has different numbers, so you still do the working yourself.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\">3 ^ 4</div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "^ means <strong>raised to the power of</strong>. The second number says how many times to write the first number.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\">3 ^ <span class=\"wt-hl\">4</span></div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Write 3 four times, with * between each one.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\"><span class=\"wt-hl\">3 * 3 * 3 * 3</span></div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Multiply one step at a time: 3 * 3 = 9. Then 9 * 3 = 27. Then 27 * 3 = 81.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\">9 &rarr; 27 &rarr; <span class=\"wt-hl\">81</span></div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "So 3 ^ 4 = 81. It is <strong>not</strong> 3 * 4 = 12. That is a different operator.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\">3 ^ 4 = <span class=\"wt-hl\">81</span></div><div class=\"wt-note\">3 * 4 = 12 is multiply, not power.</div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Now do your question the same way: write the first number, the second number of times, and multiply.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\">? ^ ?</div>"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "do-now-2",
   "label": "Do Now: Data Types (2 of 2)",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11op-do-now-2",
   "validatorKey": "y11op_do_now_2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Data Types (2 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does a program need to know the data type?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It must know what kind of value it stores and what it can do with it, such as maths with numbers.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">From 8.1 L2. Cambridge IGCSE 0478/21, November 2023, Question 3.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">Write the most appropriate data type for each description. Not all data types will be used.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">BOOLEAN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">CHAR</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">REAL</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">STRING</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-do-now-2-a\">(a) a whole number [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-do-now-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Data Types (2 of 2) part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-do-now-2-b\">(b) a single letter [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-do-now-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Data Types (2 of 2) part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-do-now-2-c\">(c) a word or phrase [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-do-now-2-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-c\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Data Types (2 of 2) part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-do-now-2-d\">(d) a number with two decimal places [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-do-now-2-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-d\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Data Types (2 of 2) part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11op-do-now-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11op-do-now-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>",
   "walkthrough": {
    "title": "Walk me through it: match data to a data type",
    "steps": [
     {
      "text": "A similar description: <strong>whether a door is open</strong>. We will find its data type.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\">whether a door is open</div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Ask the first question: is it only TRUE or FALSE? A door is open or it is not. <strong>Yes.</strong>",
      "visual": "<table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px\"><tr class=\"wt-hl\"><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it only TRUE or FALSE?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>Yes</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it a number?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong></strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Does the number have a decimal point?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong></strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it text: one letter, or many letters?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong></strong></td></tr></table>"
     },
     {
      "text": "A value that is only TRUE or FALSE is <strong>BOOLEAN</strong>. You can stop asking.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-big\">door open &rarr; <span class=\"wt-hl\">BOOLEAN</span></div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "If the answer is No, ask the next question: is it a number? Then: does it have a decimal point?",
      "visual": "<table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it only TRUE or FALSE?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>No</strong></td></tr><tr class=\"wt-hl\"><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it a number?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Does the number have a decimal point?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it text: one letter, or many letters?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong></strong></td></tr></table>"
     },
     {
      "text": "If it is not a number, it is text. Ask: is it one letter, or many letters?",
      "visual": "<table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it only TRUE or FALSE?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>No</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it a number?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>No</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Does the number have a decimal point?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong></strong></td></tr><tr class=\"wt-hl\"><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it text: one letter, or many letters?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr></table>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Now ask the questions, in order, for each description in your question. One data type is not used.",
      "visual": "<table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it only TRUE or FALSE?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it a number?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Does the number have a decimal point?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Is it text: one letter, or many letters?</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>?</strong></td></tr></table>"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
