  {
   "id": "title",
   "label": "Relational and Logical Operators",
   "content": "<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">8.1 Programming Concepts</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Relational and Logical Operators</h2><p>Year 11</p></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Today:</strong> a <strong>relational operator</strong> compares two values. The answer is TRUE or FALSE.</li><li><strong>Then:</strong> <strong>logical operators</strong>: AND, OR and NOT.</li><li><strong>Activities:</strong> trace a program, then write IF statements and run them.</li></ul><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does a program need to compare values?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>To make a decision: pass or fail, the right password or the wrong one, game over or keep playing.</p></div></details>"
  },
  {
   "id": "relational",
   "label": "Six Relational Operators",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Six Relational Operators</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: Age is 15. Is Age &lt; 18 TRUE or FALSE? Is Age &gt; 18 TRUE or FALSE?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Age &lt; 18 is <strong>TRUE</strong>: 15 is less than 18.</p><p>Age &gt; 18 is <strong>FALSE</strong>: 15 is not greater than 18.</p></div></details><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Operator</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">It means</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Example</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">When Age is 15</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>=</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">equal to</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age = 15</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>&lt;</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">less than</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &lt; 18</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>&lt;=</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">less than or equal to</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &lt;= 15</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>&gt;</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">greater than</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &gt; 18</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>&gt;=</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">greater than or equal to</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &gt;= 16</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>&lt;&gt;</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">not equal to</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &lt;&gt; 15</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td></tr></table><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>The answer is always <strong>TRUE</strong> or <strong>FALSE</strong>: a BOOLEAN value.</li><li>In a program: <code>IF Age &lt; 18 THEN</code></li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "id": "check-rel",
   "label": "Check: TRUE or FALSE?",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11op-check-rel",
   "validatorKey": "y11op_check_rel",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: TRUE or FALSE?</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is &lt;&gt; made of two symbols?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Not equal means less than or greater than: &lt; and &gt; together.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Score is 12. Is each condition TRUE or FALSE?</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-rel-a\">(a) Score &gt; 10 [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-rel-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-rel-a\" aria-label=\"Check: TRUE or FALSE? part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-rel-b\">(b) Score &lt;&gt; 12 [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-rel-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-rel-b\" aria-label=\"Check: TRUE or FALSE? part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-rel-c\">(c) Score &lt;= 11 [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-rel-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-rel-c\" aria-label=\"Check: TRUE or FALSE? part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-rel-d\">(d) Write the operator that means not equal to. [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-rel-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-rel-d\" aria-label=\"Check: TRUE or FALSE? part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11op-check-rel-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11op-check-rel-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "compare-gt",
   "label": "Compare: > and >=",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Compare: &gt; and &gt;=</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Look at the row where Mark is 50. Why are the two answers different?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>&gt;= includes 50 itself. &gt; only starts above 50.</p><p>50 is the value <strong>on the line</strong>. That is where the two operators are different.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Mark</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Mark &gt; 50</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Mark &gt;= 50</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">49</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">50</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">51</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr></table></div><div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>\"more than 50\"</strong> means <code>Mark &gt; 50</code>.</li><li><strong>\"50 or more\"</strong> means <code>Mark &gt;= 50</code>.</li><li>Always test the value on the line.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "check-bound",
   "label": "Check: On the Line",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11op-check-bound",
   "validatorKey": "y11op_check_bound",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: On the Line</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why do exam questions often use the value on the line?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It is where &gt; and &gt;= give different answers, so it finds the mistake.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Age is 18.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-bound-a\">(a) Is Age &gt; 18 TRUE or FALSE? [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-bound-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-bound-a\" aria-label=\"Check: On the Line part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-bound-b\">(b) Is Age &gt;= 18 TRUE or FALSE? [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-bound-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-bound-b\" aria-label=\"Check: On the Line part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response is-line\"><label for=\"y11op-check-bound-c\">(c) Write the condition: Age is 18 or more. [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-bound-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-bound-c\" aria-label=\"Check: On the Line part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response is-line\"><label for=\"y11op-check-bound-d\">(d) Write the condition: Speed is less than 30. [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-bound-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-bound-d\" aria-label=\"Check: On the Line part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11op-check-bound-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11op-check-bound-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
  },
