   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Activity 1: Trace the Passes</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does 50 add to Passes, but 49 does not?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>50 &gt;= 50 is TRUE: 50 is equal to 50. 49 &gt;= 50 is FALSE.</p></div></details><div id=\"y11op-embed-1\" class=\"lesson-embed\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "logical",
   "label": "Three Logical Operators",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Three Logical Operators</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: Age is 15. Is Age &gt; 12 AND Age &lt; 20 TRUE or FALSE?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Age &gt; 12 is TRUE. Age &lt; 20 is TRUE.</p><p>Both are TRUE, so the answer is <strong>TRUE</strong>.</p></div></details><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Operator</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">It means</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Example</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">When Age is 15</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>AND</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE only when <strong>both</strong> conditions are TRUE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &gt; 12 AND Age &lt; 20</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>OR</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE when <strong>at least one</strong> condition is TRUE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &lt; 10 OR Age &gt; 13</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>NOT</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>changes</strong> TRUE to FALSE, and FALSE to TRUE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">NOT Age = 15</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td></tr></table><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>A logical operator joins two conditions, or changes one.</li><li>Work out each condition first. Then use AND, OR or NOT.</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "id": "check-logic",
   "label": "Check: AND, OR, NOT",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11op-check-logic",
   "validatorKey": "y11op_check_logic",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: AND, OR, NOT</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why work out each condition before AND or OR?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>AND and OR join two answers. You need both answers first.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">X is 8. Is each condition TRUE or FALSE?</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-logic-a\">(a) X &gt; 5 AND X &lt; 10 [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-logic-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-logic-a\" aria-label=\"Check: AND, OR, NOT part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-logic-b\">(b) X &lt; 5 OR X &gt; 10 [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-logic-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-logic-b\" aria-label=\"Check: AND, OR, NOT part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-logic-c\">(c) NOT X = 8 [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-logic-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-logic-c\" aria-label=\"Check: AND, OR, NOT part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11op-check-logic-d\">(d) X = 8 OR X = 9 [1]</label><input id=\"y11op-check-logic-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-logic-d\" aria-label=\"Check: AND, OR, NOT part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11op-check-logic-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11op-check-logic-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "compare-andor",
   "label": "Compare: AND and OR",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Compare: AND and OR</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Look at the OR column. Why is it TRUE for every age?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Every age is greater than 12 or less than 20, so OR is always TRUE here.</p><p>To check a value is <strong>between</strong> two numbers, use AND.</p></div></details><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &gt; 12</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &lt; 20</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &gt; 12 AND Age &lt; 20</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Age &gt; 12 OR Age &lt; 20</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">10</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">15</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">25</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">FALSE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr></table><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>AND</strong>: both must be TRUE. Use it for <strong>between</strong>.</li><li><strong>OR</strong>: one is enough. Use it for <strong>either one</strong>.</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "id": "exam-le",
   "label": "Exam Question: Which Operator?",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y11op-exam-le",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Which Operator?</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Which option can you cross out first, and why?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>OR: it is a logical operator. It joins two conditions and does not compare values.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/21, November 2023, Question 1.</p><div id=\"y11op-exam-le\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "Tick one box to show which operator means less than or equal to.",
     "options": [
      "OR",
      "<",
      "<=",
      ">="
     ],
     "correct": 2,
     "explain": "<= means less than or equal to. < is less than only. OR is a logical operator."
    }
   ]
