  {
   "id": "exam-profit",
   "label": "Exam Question: Find the Errors",
   "type": "self-marked-response",
   "containerId": "y11op-exam-profit",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Find the Errors</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Line 11 uses OR and it is correct. Why is OR wrong on line 06?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Line 06 must work out the profit only when both prices are not zero, so it needs AND. Line 11 stops when either price is zero, so OR is right.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/22, March 2024, Question 5(a). An algorithm has been written in pseudocode to calculate the profit when an item is sold. Values for cost price and selling price are input, the profit is calculated (selling price - cost price) and output. The input of zero for either value stops the algorithm.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">01&nbsp;&nbsp;REPEAT</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">02&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Enter cost price \"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">03&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Cost</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">04&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Enter selling price \"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Sell</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">06&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Cost &lt;&gt; 0 OR Sell &lt;&gt; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">07&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">08&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Profit &lt;- Sell - Cost</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">09&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Profit is \", Profit</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">10&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">11&nbsp;&nbsp;UNTIL Cost = 0 OR Sell = 0</div></div></div><div><div id=\"y11op-exam-profit\"></div></div></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "errors",
     "prompt": "Identify the line numbers of three errors in the pseudocode and suggest corrections. [3]",
     "marks": 3,
     "modelAnswer": "Line 05: OUTPUT should be INPUT. Line 06: OR should be AND. Line 10: NEXT should be ENDIF."
    }
   ]
